From: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: ipq9574: expose read-only analog state in debugfs

The QCA8081 copper PHY can report a good 1G link while no SGMII
frames cross the PHY/host PCS boundary. The existing PCS debugfs
snapshot reports PCS mode, calibration and MII link, but omits the
PLL reset control, external PHY reference clock output enable and
link detection source.

Include those three existing register values in the existing
read-only snapshot. This does not program registers, change link
recovery, consume read-clear packet counters or induce an experiment.

The reference output bit and reset control register are diagnostic
configuration readbacks, not proof of a physically locked CDR.
The next matched healthy/faulted boot comparison must determine
whether these fields differ.

Signed-off-by: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -1339,6 +1339,9 @@ static int ipq_pcs_snapshot_show(struct
 		{ "mode_ctrl", PCS_MODE_CTRL },
 		{ "misc2", PCS_MISC2 },
 		{ "vco_cal_ctrl", PCS_VCO_CAL_CTRL },
+		{ "pll_reset", PCS_PLL_RESET },
+		{ "clkout_50m_ctrl", PCS_CLKOUT_50M_CTRL },
+		{ "link_detect", PCS_LINK_DETECT },
 	};
 	struct ipq_pcs *qpcs = s->private;
 	unsigned int val;
